<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caranus of Macedon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">trad. 808 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caranus was, according to later Greek writers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theopompus">Theopompus</a> and Diodorus, the founder of the Argead royal house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>, a descendant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heracles">Heracles</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a>, traditionally dated to the 9th or 8th century BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thucydides">Thucydides</a> do not mention him and name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perdiccas">Perdiccas</a> I as founder, so he is generally regarded as a legendary figure added to lengthen the royal genealogy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caranus-of-macedon.jpg" alt="Caranus of Macedon" width="250" height="126" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aigai-_Before_520-500_BCE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
